  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Chhathilal Gupta vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 9 June,",
    "facts": "This is first application under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure on behalf of the applicant, who is in jail since 06.04.2021 in connection with Crime No.105/2021 registered at Police Station- Vijay Nagar, District- Jabalpur (MP) for the offence under Sections 420 and 272 of Indian Panel Code and Sections 51, 52 and 58 of Food Safety and Standards Act. Learned Senior Counsel appearing for the applicant submitted that no offence under Section 420 of Indian Penal Code is made out against the applicant. It is further submitted that applicant was found in possession of ghee which was said to be adulterated. On being found in possession of ghee, no offence under Section 420 of IPC will be made out against the applicant. It is also submitted that no jail sentence has been prescribed for offence under Sections 51, 52 and 58 of Food Safety and Standards Act and only fine is prescribed for the same.",
